{
  "_comment": [
    "What every theme token resolves to, per preset, captured from a real browser.",
    "",
    "This exists so the token consolidation can prove it changed nothing. The",
    "families alias each other through fallback chains (--settings-* falls back to",
    "--ws-*, which falls back to a literal), and 82 tokens are defined in more than",
    "one place, so a change that looks local can quietly alter a preset three files",
    "away. Diffing against this file names the token and the preset immediately.",
    "",
    "Values are read from the browser rather than resolved by hand: reimplementing",
    "the cascade is exactly the kind of guess that makes a safety net lie.",
    "",
    "To recapture after an INTENTIONAL change, see theme-tokens.test.mjs."
  ],
  "capturedAt": "2026-08-01",
